#uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407298 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "567abe3c-003e-5470-895b-6e4de6668d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460281} {:answer/id #uuid "42a6b8b5-f337-585c-81c8-58ef0adc78c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460282}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460281} :answer-field/id #uuid "539f1f0a-a5c7-5cf1-8dfe-991c5ed6a3c9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "229a4b0e-7cc8-578e-9c98-62c05f0575cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460283} {:answer/id #uuid "420109c7-1b02-5fdd-bd56-6921fde84d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460284}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460283} :answer-field/id #uuid "759a1a61-0534-5515-a7d7-778c990a26c4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a98d4383-44c4-517a-8eb0-cc5ae603ebcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460285} {:answer/id #uuid "0c907cc0-6af1-5efa-95fa-10890d40d058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460286}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460286} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e48dc1a-6694-5774-95fd-e6de685299f0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8098b383-f4a9-5d0e-9352-b359bad47678" :question/math-academy-id "q-80430" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7db51d6af763e8853f815feb6e74b88d0ca9a19e79c42b3a42da4e8b088f93c.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles I and II do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle III covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407301}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407299 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d87facea-76c9-53bf-b25e-e7acd8a0848f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472616} {:answer/id #uuid "34788671-40c0-55de-9282-705047e61c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472617} :answer-field/id #uuid "13cca8d7-a733-550e-ab33-1ebcc8cc6ba3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb2a430-1b20-5cd8-889c-8397d5f66f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472618} {:answer/id #uuid "facde33f-6a68-5c26-a7d0-f157550ab480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472619}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472619} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6b1f945-9ba0-5e99-9ab4-a0c22108dd3f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f4df998-df9d-5be1-85e2-6c7fe20e4d11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472620} {:answer/id #uuid "94aa333b-da6a-5843-999a-18b8e9d9555f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472621}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472620} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b668eb0-a01c-5c4c-9775-6cc00549cbbd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "04b43074-9710-54c1-a656-7d7797008d68" :question/math-academy-id "q-129786" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9d66cb97b9e04367ce2250e5156eaa9daaf42fadb395220e0464bca687e91908.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,4]$\n- ${∬}_{R}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-4,4]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407302}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407300 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e019259c-a480-51c7-adee-7e64d30db325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460275} {:answer/id #uuid "3c62bbae-8481-50c2-900d-f50750addcab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460276}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460275} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed25a22e-c812-5c51-97bf-3f552b015487" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f843948-205f-56d3-9549-f072aa94f578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460277} {:answer/id #uuid "b8af677d-062c-5280-a8a3-61adf659040c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460278}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460278} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f5cff7-ebff-5f64-bebb-f05d813e5cf0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd0c58ef-21d5-557b-b1f3-8d8357abcf16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460279} {:answer/id #uuid "31b0c3fa-e8ff-5c10-b771-f69f3886b0f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460280}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186460279} :answer-field/id #uuid "43970d5a-70f7-5eaf-9c95-866b3155b96e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ca2c9d4-83c1-5596-b062-1537df902124" :question/math-academy-id "q-80425" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d09a23a1ae9f737c7f19ba83d6d20c3fbcea3c7deb71fa307264c90afabc6580.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/16/1620acdcfd3783df478322ebe5e81cb274d908db12d9c8bdc701fe21070b828f.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and III. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function II equals $\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+{x}^{2}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407298}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407301 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d785f01e-c01b-508b-a7e4-0b68e3819afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473512} {:answer/id #uuid "72475eb4-0b35-5d4b-9ea7-4c75ae1d9bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473513} :answer-field/id #uuid "7063df18-38c8-5001-85dc-c37c2a884180" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45915786-bde2-58ed-b09f-01d02dd4ab1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473514} {:answer/id #uuid "db2767a5-0290-566a-8860-446c19d11819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473515}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473514} :answer-field/id #uuid "9428d01a-a858-5759-ad6e-dec6825a2e03" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474152} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20decd90-c71f-5b9c-af2d-3a173c83d963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473516} {:answer/id #uuid "025119c3-228a-5031-89d8-d102fe48b0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473517}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186473516} :answer-field/id #uuid "31799862-7294-50e6-9e5a-cbd879317060" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" :question/math-academy-id "q-86866" :question/problem "![](images/51/51706be38cc1c72079fe702c899b575ea53ba4d85e7990a6aa81f20dc8da4de3.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. ${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [0,3]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{R}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-5,5]\\times [0,3]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :step/id #uuid "5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407299}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407302 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "034d7503-b6f8-527c-a973-ac2bfc867df1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472622} {:answer/id #uuid "77d96fda-e870-55c8-b23f-4d1d5eb0e5f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472623}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472623} :answer-field/id #uuid "256d9380-5a22-5d58-bc62-7da50bb3ece8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f3b95a-f8ca-5464-96e2-8800e62a2417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472624} {:answer/id #uuid "50306918-6a2a-5e3c-a5ab-150d520b00cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472625}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472624} :answer-field/id #uuid "16d53d61-4f6d-56eb-96a8-a48708fcd15a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "642ff713-a98e-574b-ab8d-f4ec58c4a354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472626} {:answer/id #uuid "f07b0134-b33f-5f41-9115-502b58e12756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472627}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186472627} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f28af97-dc10-5715-ba3e-f26a28eab3f5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "bbe5a871-1924-5655-ad62-5cf32208bd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-129908" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-1$ and $y=2-|x|.$ If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n- **I.** ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n- **II.** ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n- **III.** ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/1a/1a5369b58b14444c5ea0ce4bb36954d1d0b7964dcef4e95f9cc527694b3a9e4f.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- Functions I and III equal $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ on $D$ and equal $0$ outside $D.$\n\n- We cannot use function II. The function is not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(1,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the function is nonzero at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :step/id #uuid "98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb"}] :activity/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407276}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425932} :activity/id #uuid "c1b2bf8a-6e24-5f4d-b8cf-9b6296b332cb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049229 :topic/id #uuid "e52ab899-5fcb-50d2-afee-4830a70f16df" :topic/math-academy-id 2616} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425932 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c96195d-9858-594d-bb72-8ff337d223f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474906} {:answer/id #uuid "ac21b789-f73c-5a27-a558-3259fd8be378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474907}] :a